# Code owners for security-sensitive review machinery.
#
# These paths define the criteria and prompts that gate every PR. A change to
# them changes what the review agents and CI accept, so they require explicit
# owner review. Refs #1967.
#
# Note: the former `.claude/review-axes/` was moved to
# `.claude/skills/review/references/` in PR #2043; pin the current path.

# Canonical /review axis criteria (CI prompts are generated from these).
/.claude/skills/review/references/        @rjmurillo

# Generated CI review prompts (pr-quality gate, per role).
/.github/prompts/pr-quality-gate-*.md     @rjmurillo
/.github/prompts/pr-quality.*.prompt.md   @rjmurillo

# Shared library backing the AI review gates and the plugin hook shims. The
# canonical packages live under scripts/; .claude/lib/ is the binplaced copy
# (ADR-109 B5, build/scripts/lib_mirror.py). Pin both so gate-logic changes
# (verdict.py merge rules) or hook-utility changes cannot bypass owner review.
/scripts/ai_review_common/                @rjmurillo
/.claude/lib/ai_review_common/            @rjmurillo
/scripts/hook_utilities/                  @rjmurillo
/.claude/lib/hook_utilities/              @rjmurillo
/scripts/github_core/                     @rjmurillo
/.claude/lib/github_core/                 @rjmurillo

# Template-owned skill files (ADR-108). A template under templates/skills/ is
# the only class permitted to write under .claude/ during the build, and the
# pilot-scope test pins which names may. Widening either needs owner review.
/templates/skills/                                            @rjmurillo
/templates/agents/                                            @rjmurillo
/templates/rules/                                             @rjmurillo
/templates/hooks/                                             @rjmurillo
/templates/platforms/                                         @rjmurillo
/tests/build_scripts/test_skill_templates_pilot_scope.py      @rjmurillo

# Enforcement paths (ADR-101 Phase 0 item 3, issue #5244).
#
# ADR-101's invariant is that a gate protecting artifacts at plane N must
# compute its verdict above N, from evidence the gated actor cannot forge.
# Everything below decides whether a change is allowed to merge, so a change
# to one of these paths is a change to the gate itself and needs owner review.
#
# scripts/workflows/ is the sharpest entry. determine_should_run_from_filters.py
# decides six of the eight contexts pinned in scripts/ci/ruleset_required_contexts.py,
# it is editable in the same pull request it gates, and the tests that would
# catch such an edit run inside the jobs the edit disables. Until that decision
# moves to a base-ref job (issue #5244 item 6), owner review is the only control
# standing in front of it.
#
# This list is a seed, not the control. ADR-101's typed dependency closure
# (Phase 1) computes the real edge set and fails closed on an edge that does
# not resolve. An earlier hand-written revision of this same list omitted
# scripts/workflows/, which is precisely why the closure exists.
#
# tests/ci/test_codeowners_enforcement_paths.py pins every entry below.
/.github/workflows/                       @rjmurillo
/.github/actions/                         @rjmurillo
/scripts/validation/                      @rjmurillo
/scripts/ci/                              @rjmurillo
/scripts/workflows/                       @rjmurillo
/tests/.test_durations                    @rjmurillo
/build/scripts/                           @rjmurillo
/lefthook.yml                             @rjmurillo
/.github/CODEOWNERS                       @rjmurillo
# Issue #5636: the drift allowlist decides which generated agent files may
# differ from their templates, and the validator that reads it is the gate.
# An entry added in the same PR it excuses needs an owner's review.
/.agents/governance/drift-allowlist.json  @rjmurillo
/build/drift_allowlist.py                 @rjmurillo
/build/generate_agents.py                 @rjmurillo
# Issue #5636, decision D17: the bypass allowlist authorizes SKIP_ toggles and
# continue-on-error steps. An entry added in the PR it excuses needs the owner.
/.agents/governance/bypass-allowlist.json @rjmurillo
/scripts/validation/bypass_allowlist.py   @rjmurillo
/scripts/validation/check_bypass_allowlist.py @rjmurillo
# Issue #5636, ADR-113: the promotion exceptions file and its loader decide
# which release findings may be accepted. An entry added in the PR it excuses
# needs the owner.
/.agents/governance/promotion-exceptions.json @rjmurillo
/scripts/validation/promotion_exceptions.py @rjmurillo
# Issue #5636, ADR-113 decision 3: the applicability table says which validators
# a promotion must see. A row added or dropped in the PR it excuses needs the owner.
/.agents/governance/promotion-applicability.json @rjmurillo
/scripts/validation/promotion_applicability.py @rjmurillo

# Issue #5636, ADR-113 decision 2: the evidence a promotion reads is written by
# this emitter and uploaded by this action. A change to either decides what a
# validator job claims, so it needs the owner.
/scripts/validation/emit_validator_evidence.py @rjmurillo
/.github/actions/upload-validator-evidence/ @rjmurillo

# ADR-101 requirement 2a publisher (issue #5245). The workflow holds the App
# credential and the scripts decide what it publishes, so a change to either
# needs owner review before it can reach the key.
/.github/workflows/adr101-publisher.yml     @rjmurillo
/scripts/ci/adr101_publisher.py             @rjmurillo
/scripts/ci/adr101_publisher_execute.py     @rjmurillo
/scripts/ci/adr101_publisher_github.py      @rjmurillo
/scripts/ci/adr101_publisher_inputs.py      @rjmurillo

# Issue #5636, ADR-113 decision 5: these programs decide which workflow runs and
# artifacts count as evidence. A change to them changes what a promotion trusts.
/scripts/validation/promotion_provenance.py @rjmurillo
/scripts/validation/promotion_fetch.py @rjmurillo
/scripts/validation/fetch_promotion_evidence.py @rjmurillo

# Issue #5636, ADR-113 Resolved Question 3: these programs choose and read the
